    "description": "<table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:1em; border:1px solid #999; font-size:90%; text-align:center; background:#363636\">\n <tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td><i>This article details the Rail Cannon <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_System\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Weapon System\">Weapon System</a> found in the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Clone Wars Campaign Guide\">Clone Wars Campaign Guide</a>. You may be looking for the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Homebrew_Content\" title=\"Homebrew Content\">Homebrew Content</a> Weapon System of the same name, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Rail_Cannon_System\" title=\"Rail Cannon System\">Rail Cannon System</a>.</i></td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide</a></i></p><p><b>Size Restriction:</b> Gargantuan or Larger</p><p>Rail Cannons deliver explosive warheads at super-high velocity, inflicting damage via both the payload and the kinetic energy of the impact.</p><p>Like <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Mass-Driver_Cannons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mass-Driver Cannons\">Mass-Driver Cannons</a>, Rail Cannons can only be mounted on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicles\" title=\"Vehicles\">Vehicles</a> of Gargantuan size or larger because of their intense recoil.</p>",
